<title>SWITZERLAND: SAirGroup to write off min 185 mln Sfr.</title>
<headline>SAirGroup to write off min 185 mln Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>SAirGroup chief executive Philippe Bruggisser said Sabena's 8.9 billion Belgian franc loss in 1996 would hurt Swissair's 1996 profit and the issue was whether or not to write off this amount or more on its balance sheet.</p>
<p>The loss is equivalent to around 370 million Swiss francs. Swissair owns 49.5 percent of Sabena, which means a loss on Swissair's accounts of 185 million Swiss francs.</p>
</text>
